WEBVTT

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:05.850
Is this some joke, Marie?

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.820
Over half this box of cigars
you sold me are just damn carrots!

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.820
I may be a horse beastman,
but carrots are no replacement for cigars!

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.660
I want my money back!

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:20.660
I showed you a photo of it first, right?

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.120
I said, "You want this?"

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:28.040
You looked at this and said, "Yes."
I didn't swindle you.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:32.170
Got it? Now get your horse face home.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:33.630
Bye.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:43.560
What the hell is that?

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.480
What's wrong, Marie?

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:50.020
How should I know?
That guy suddenly flew into a rage!

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.520
See you later!

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.570
I'm out of here like a rabbit,
even though I'm a mink!

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:57.110
Shirou, is that another one?

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.820
-It's just like with Yaba.
-Got it!

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:10.750
-Now!
-Yes!

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.760
Mayor, there is
a rampaging beastman in town.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.260
Mr. Ogami is handling it.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.640
All right. Let's go there too.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.480
Chairman Alan?
I'm sorry, I'm very busy right now.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:33.310
I know.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.320
I'd like to speak with you about that.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.710
-Is he going to be okay?
-Yes. I won't kill him this time.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.010
All right!

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:04.430
What?

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:14.980
What are those?

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:21.970
Shirou!

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.590
I'm fine.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:39.690
Let's go after them.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:51.950
The Medical Center?

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:54.080
They're here for sure.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:56.210
Any further is dangerous.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.130
You should go back to...

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:02.260
-Hey! I'm talking--
-I won't stand for getting shot at,

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.090
and I want to know what those were.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:06.630
Besides, you're all worked up.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.350
You always lose your cool
when it comes to Sylvasta.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.430
It's way more dangerous
to let you go in alone.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:16.270
Let's go. I found a way to sneak in
the last time I was here.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:35.330
I thought you could sneak in this way.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:38.790
<i>Ogami,</i>

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:41.000
<i>this is a medical facility.</i>

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:44.130
<i>Would you please refrain</i>
<i>from getting violent?</i>

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.130
Alan?

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:47.010
<i>Hi, Michiru.</i>

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:50.050
This is perfect.
I have questions for you anyway.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.470
<i>I figured.</i>

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.770
<i>You there, show them in.</i>

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.730
I didn't know about this facility.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.150
-This is odd.
-What's odd?

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:07.280
There are only humans here.

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.160
Medi-Cen is supposed to be for beastmen.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:12.160
-Is something fishy?
-Yes.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.160
I intended to keep this all under wraps.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.710
But I didn't know you two were involved.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:22.670
Then those devices are from Medi-Cen?
What the heck are they?

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:24.920
They're Engel Maschines,

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:27.800
medical devices for subduing beastmen.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:29.510
Medical devices?

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:30.970
They shot at her!

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:32.760
I'm sorry about that.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:36.100
They're made to subdue beastmen
who have turned savage.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:39.350
They tranquilized that horse beastman
to subdue him.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:42.560
They mistook you for a beastman
who needed to be subdued, Michiru.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:44.520
Those were real bullets.

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:48.070
Since I wasn't around,
my subordinates dispatched them.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:51.780
They were improperly equipped.
I am truly very sorry.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:55.330
I'll take steps to make sure
this doesn't happen again.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.910
The subdued beastman
is undergoing treatment here.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:00.460
Another beastman experiment, huh?

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.250
That kind of thing is unacceptable
in Anima-City.

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:06.170
It looks like you'll chew me to bits
before I can answer.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.800
You'd better believe it!

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:09.470
Shirou, calm down!

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:11.800
What are you trying to do in this city?

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.930
I don't want any of your crafty excuses.

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:15.260
All right.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:18.520
It looks like I need
to tell you the truth.

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:22.150
We need samples of beastmen
who've turned savage.

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:25.150
<i>It may seem rather harsh,</i>
<i>but we don't have time.</i>

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.400
Inject the experimental drug.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:30.950
What are you doing?

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:34.320
Would you please put away
those fangs and claws for a moment?

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.910
I don't want my windpipe ripped out
because you flew into a rage.

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:41.960
The way things are going,
Anima-City will end up being destroyed.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:44.420
Just like what happened in Nirvasyl.

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:49.170
You know about that town?

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:52.880
<i>The general who led the army then</i>
<i>was...</i>

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:54.840
<i>Raymond Sylvasta.</i>

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:59.100
-"Sylvasta"?
-That's right.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.600
My ancestor.

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:14.950
Will you let your anger get the best
of you and get Michiru hurt too?

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:16.490
You bastard!

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:19.040
I simply want you to listen calmly.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.120
Ogami, you've been mistaken.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:26.130
Humans didn't attack the beastmen
in Nirvasyl.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.000
It was the opposite.

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:31.130
They were protecting themselves
from the attacking beastmen.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:33.300
When the human army arrived,

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:35.800
the beastmen
were already killing each other.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:37.180
That's absurd!

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.680
How could humans have defeated beastmen?

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.640
It was 1,000 years ago.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:43.850
There were no firearms or explosives.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:46.900
With nothing more than dull swords,
heavy shields, and spears,

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:49.980
do you think they could defend
against attacks from agile beastmen?

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:53.780
Since the beastmen had fought
among themselves and were injured,

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.200
the humans were able to finish them off.

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:58.410
How dare you talk like you were there?

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:00.280
You were there, so let me ask you.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.620
Doesn't it sound like
that's what happened?

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:06.040
I know you're a survivor of Nirvasyl.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:07.880
How did you know?

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:10.800
I had you checked out long ago.

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:12.550
And that's not all.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:14.340
The story of Silver Wolf

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:17.550
seeking vengeance
was passed down through my family.

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.260
You quit your meaningless vengeance,
so you must understand.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:25.100
At that time, was it humans
who slaughtered beastmen,

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.270
or did enraged beastmen attack
other beastmen,

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:30.110
like Yaba did?

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:37.110
Maybe so, but...

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:44.370
Originally, groups of the same species
of beastmen lived in different areas.

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:48.540
<i>Different species of beastmen</i>
<i>weren't used to living with each other.</i>

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:54.300
<i>The stress from multiple species invading</i>
<i>your habitat accumulates subconsciously.</i>

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:58.130
<i>In that situation,</i>
<i>if there is a powerful mental shock,</i>

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:01.430
<i>the enrage switch in</i>
<i>beast deoxyribonucleic acid is set off,</i>

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:03.720
<i>and their fight instincts take over.</i>

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:07.020
<i>It's called beast deoxyribonucleic acid</i>
<i>rampage syndrome,</i>

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:09.980
<i>also known as Nirvasyl Syndrome.</i>

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:15.530
I've analyzed the beast deoxyribonucleic
acid of the beastmen in this city.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:18.950
Their aggressive cerebral factor values
have increased rapidly.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:23.410
If the population increases further,
they'll be pushed beyond the limit.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:27.330
Oh, I see. That's why they're trying
to move out the Church.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.880
What about the mayor?
Does she know about this?

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:32.670
Of course, I've told her.

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:34.840
She understands the situation.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:40.260
<i>We merely built this city</i>

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.760
<i>so that beastmen could live in peace</i>

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:45.770
with the same rights as humans have.

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:47.220
But...

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:50.600
was it all a mistake?

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:55.440
So these last ten years,
I was just building hell for beastmen?

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:58.150
Can you be sure Chairman Alan is right?

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:00.820
I checked the data from Sylvasta.

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:03.490
Alan's hypothesis is correct.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:06.660
Contact Prime Minister Shiramizu
immediately!

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:07.910
Right.

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:13.710
The reason we built this Medical Center
in Anima-City

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:16.670
was to develop a vaccine
for Nirvasyl Syndrome.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:19.630
It's easy to get beastmen samples here.

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:22.760
Wait! Is that vaccine you're making...

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.720
That's right. It's a medicine
to turn beastmen into humans.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:28.430
<i>Beast deoxyribonucleic acid</i>
<i>termination vaccine.</i>

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.690
<i>By stopping the morphing of beastmen,</i>
<i>Nirvasyl Syndrome will never happen.</i>

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:35.560
Is that the medicine that will cure me
of my beastman disease?

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:37.940
Yes, that's what it is.

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:39.070
You're kidding!

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:42.070
You want beastmen
to give up on being beastmen?

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:44.200
We'll never be damn humans!

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:52.960
Shirou!

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:58.670
They're tranquilizer darts.
Will you calm down now, please?

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:01.630
Humans are always like this.

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:05.260
They suppress beastmen by force.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:08.010
At this rate,
the beastmen will all kill one another!

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:09.140
Do you want that?

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:12.270
Humans have no right

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:14.520
to make that decision!

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.360
Shirou!

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:23.320
That's a surprise.
Even those tranquilizers don't work.

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:27.370
Beast deoxyribonucleic acid activity
decreasing. Terminating state.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:30.200
Excellent! It's a success!

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:36.330
Stop it! Cut it out, I said!

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:38.000
Why should I stop?

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:41.340
I won't let humans make a drug
that will eliminate beastmen!

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:45.720
You saw for yourself, Shirou,
how this guy and Mr. Yaba became enraged!

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:49.220
You want everyone to end up like that?
Everyone killing each other?

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:50.470
You butt out!

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:53.230
They will all become humans
at the hands of humans!

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.520
But at least they will survive!

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:59.480
If you destroy this place,
everyone will lose the chance to survive!

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:01.400
-Out of my way!
-I'm not budging!

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.990
You want a drug
to turn back into a human that badly?

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:05.490
What?

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.870
You just want to turn back into a human.

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:11.580
-How can you...
-You're nothing more than a human!

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:14.040
You don't know
what it's like to be a beastman!

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:18.420
You're always like this!
You always jump to conclusions!

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:22.250
How the heck could I understand
how the legendary Silver Wolf feels?

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:25.170
Does living 1,000 years make you
that great?

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:29.010
In those 1,000 years, you've simply become
fanatical in your hatred of humans!

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:32.140
What? How dare you say that!

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:39.060
Don't move!

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:40.560
It's Mr. Tachiki.

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:44.570
I got a report that a suspicious character
was on a rampage at the Medical Center.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:46.780
I never thought it would be you, Ogami.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:48.660
Unfortunately,

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:51.620
he's the one who destroyed this place.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:54.580
Ogami, I'm taking you down to the station.

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:57.790
You're under arrest
for destroying property.

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:00.960
You think I'll let you arrest me
without a fight?

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.300
Come on. Don't let it come to that.

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:05.460
I don't want to fight you.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:07.260
I'm only doing my job.

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:10.510
If you fight the police,
you're nothing more than a criminal!

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:12.810
You'll be just like those terrorists!

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:23.570
Shirou.

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:25.650
After him!

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:28.650
Let the police take care of this.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:31.320
-But...
-It will be all right.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:33.410
He's a strong man.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:36.620
Once he calms down,
I'm sure he'll understand.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:40.080
Thank you, Michiru.

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:41.290
What?

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:44.800
You protected the devices used
in the development from him.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:48.420
That's the same as saving the lives
of many beastmen.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:51.300
You don't have to thank me.

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:54.600
Actually, Michiru,

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:57.730
I want you to help out Nazuna.

00:14:58.310 --> 00:14:59.940
-Nazuna?
-That's right.

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:04.980
I've asked her to do a job for me,
but I think she could use your help.

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:07.030
A job?

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:09.900
It's the task of saving Anima-City.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:18.080
What brings you to me?

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:20.460
The mayor wants to talk to you.

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:21.830
I figured.

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:25.540
The police are guarding
the mayor's residence. Come with me.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:31.130
Thank goodness!

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:34.300
See, Michiru's back!

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:35.260
Yes.

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.350
I'm glad I prayed to Silver Wolf.

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:41.890
The police dropped by
and said Shirou was wanted.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:43.560
She was so worried.

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:46.770
There must be a mistake, right?
Where's Shirou?

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:50.950
What?

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:00.700
Nazuna?

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:10.380
If you can live, why does it matter
if you're human or beastman?

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:14.590
I know that,
but that's not what Shirou thinks.

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:18.760
Did Alan tell you about the concert?

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:20.470
-A concert?
-That's right.

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:24.560
Until the drug can be developed,
the Church will hold a concert

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.810
to relieve the beastmen's stress.

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:29.820
The concert will be streamed
all over Anima-City!

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:34.410
-Really?
-I asked Alan to put you on my staff.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:37.320
This will be my first concert, after all.

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:40.040
Let's come up with a setlist together.

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:44.420
Nazuna, did you know
about the Nirvasyl Syndrome?

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:49.040
Yes. Alan told me to keep it a secret
from anyone who wasn't involved.

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:53.720
But you're involved now, Michiru.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:56.680
Now I've got no other secrets from you.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:59.430
-Really?
-Maybe.

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:01.180
If I still do, forgive me.

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.100
That's ridiculous.

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:04.600
Oh, well. Whatever.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:05.940
A concert, huh?

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:08.860
You're amazing, Nazuna!
You're a real pop idol now.

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:11.820
That's right. I'll become the real thing.

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:21.490
We'll make this concert a success
and save this city!

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:26.420
Michiru, I've brought you some tea.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:29.540
Actually, this isn't...

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:32.250
Silver Wolf! What are you doing here?

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:36.300
I am always with those who believe in me.

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:38.800
I will go wherever I am needed.

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:40.760
You sure switched fast.

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:43.600
Oh, yes, that's right.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:46.980
This poor girl has gone through
quite a lot lately.

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:48.770
You really are amazing, Silver Wolf.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:51.860
She will be fine.
She is sure to find the light.

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:55.030
I will be going now.
Be the best beastman you can be.

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:56.990
Be the best beastman you can be.

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:03.950
Is Silver Wolf really that great?

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:05.700
Yes, that's right.

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:10.040
But I never expected her to be
such a young girl.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.000
What?

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:13.710
That kind of trivial stuff
doesn't bother me.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.920
Just as long as Silver Wolf is with us.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:17.930
Be the best beastman you can be.

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:22.510
You went too far, Ogami.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.640
Do you know what Alan is trying to do?

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:29.140
He's trying to turn beastmen into humans!

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:32.150
-I know.
-Then why stop me?

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:35.570
Not all beastmen are willing
to remain a beastman

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:37.690
even if it means dying.

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:39.240
You're on his side too?

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:42.410
But I'll do something
to make sure it doesn't happen.

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:45.540
I'll dismantle Anima-City.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:50.370
If beastmen go on a rampage
due to living in a crowded city,

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:52.960
then we'll disperse
the beastmen living here.

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:55.710
I'm meeting
with Prime Minister Shiramizu tomorrow.

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:59.970
I plan on asking him to allow beastmen
to be dispersed throughout Japan.

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:04.890
However, if Nirvasyl Syndrome occurs
before that, then we have no choice

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:08.430
but to use the beast deoxyribonucleic acid
termination vaccine.

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:09.890
How can you say that?

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:22.070
All right. Do whatever you think is best.

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:44.600
Where did he go, huh?

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:01.070
Why are you all wet?
It hasn't been raining.

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:03.700
If you've got no business with me,
then scram.

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:05.820
I'm in a bad mood right now.

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:09.160
It figures.
The cops are after you, after all.

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:11.330
I'll give you a lift. Get in.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:13.000
I don't need one.

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:15.130
Don't talk like that.

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:17.880
I heard you fought with Sylvasta.

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:20.840
What is it you know, Ogami?

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:24.430
I know something shady is going on
in this city.

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:28.060
I wouldn't be the boss of the Family
if I didn't know that.

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:41.240
<i>I see. Yes, this is definitely</i>
<i>an urgent matter.</i>

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:45.570
<i>The mutual understanding between humans</i>
<i>and beastmen is still insufficient.</i>

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:48.490
Though this disease can be avoided,

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:51.790
if humans found out about it now,
it would just cause more fear.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:55.960
Please keep it a secret
while dispersing the beastmen.

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:58.420
I understand how you feel.

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:02.670
However, I cannot allow beastmen
to leave Anima-City.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:06.680
What's this?

00:21:07.050 --> 00:21:10.810
I've already received word
about Nirvasyl Syndrome

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:12.640
and taken steps to handle things.

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:16.140
Mayor Rosé,
there is an order for you to be seized.

00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:17.230
Seized?

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:20.020
I'll handle the rest,

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:22.610
so why don't you just take it easy
for a while?

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:24.820
Wait! Prime Minister!

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:30.660
Thank you. I appreciate your cooperation,
Prime Minister.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:37.960
Shirou?

00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:46.800
I can't believe him!

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:49.010
That stubborn old man!

00:22:48.490 --> 00:22:50.490
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
